+A run on the headless route (`worker_mode: headless` in `show`, `skills/dagq/reference/provider.md`) has no screen and takes no keys: its workspace runs only the session wrapper, so none of the `run screen` / `run send` steps above apply to it (`run screen` names its `turns/` instead, `run send` refuses it). Its ask comes from a turn that ended without a receipt or a `worker_question` after the runtime's nudges (`reason: turn_without_receipt`), or from a turn whose tools were refused three times or more (`permission_denied`), once the recovery job could not fix it, or from a recovery job's escalation of an `idle_process` alert (an ask escalated for `long_background` reads the same, but the runtime no longer raises that alert); the question ends with the last turns instead of a screen.
 
 Its options are `wait`, `stop` and `propose` (and any the job added), with no `intervene`: nobody can step into a headless session. Before answering, read what the turns did (the question's last turns, `"$DAGQ" run log RUN` for a session in the background, `"$DAGQ" timeline RUN`, `"$DAGQ" events --run RUN --full` for `turn_finished` and `permission_denials`, the turns' output under the run dir's `turns/`) and bring it to the person; then answer with one of these or an instruction.
 
